Accepted and fixed in ae28a79 (CI green: lint-test, integration, migration, build):
- C1 reference aliases bypass the shared-image check -> normalize_reference (docker.io, library/, :latest).
- G1 `trap ''` does not protect docker children (Go CLI re-enables signals via signal.Notify; systemd control-group kill)
  -> KillMode=mixed in the unit, DB restore runs under setsid in both scripts.
- C3/G2 password comparison rejects valid encoded passwords -> comparison removed (running Matomo proves the
  connection; host/user/dbname still checked). Header updated.
- C4/G8 index type/collation -> added to the fingerprint.
- C5 logger failure bypasses exit 3 -> `|| true` around logging in finish paths.
- G3 temporary .env copy with password left behind -> removed in finish_fail.
- C2 install-timer drops settings outside the example -> carried over verbatim.
- C6/G4 config_value / configured_compose_dir inherit the environment -> unset before source.
- G5 shared-image conflict exit 1 -> exit 2 (configuration/environment).
- G7 empty dump leaves .partial -> removed.
- C7/G6/G8 docs: loss window starts at the dump snapshot; --pull never on the way back; README states the switch
  upgrades Matomo when no same-version image exists; db.sh header matches db_restore_needed.
Not changed:
- G1 "TimeoutStopSec=2h is a hard cap": accepted limitation, documented in the unit; very large restores need a higher value.
